IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-nouns`

-- g8-art32-36-appeals: Part 8 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Articles 32 to 36): the Charity Tribunal, who may appeal what, the grounds of appeal, the powers of the Tribunal and of the court,
-- the Minister's power to set time limits, and the effect of a decision that takes effect from an earlier date.
-- "Who may appeal what" is a computable rule over the kind of decision (IP27: the domain record `Decision of the Commissioner`, a subject and an outcome) and the standing of the appellant.
-- The powers of the Tribunal, the court, the Minister and the Commissioner are MAY rules typed by who acts and what is done; "as it thinks fit", "satisfied" and "appears to be called for"
-- are inputs.  The time limits are the content of an Order that is not in the sources: whether an appeal is in time takes the limit as an input and refuses where none is supplied.
-- Forks: F8.4 (is the list of Article 33 closed), F8.5 (the ground of an appeal to the court), F8.6 and F8.12 (the time limit), F8.13 (who is excluded from 33(5)), F8.16 (33(2)(a) and a deregistration on the
-- charity's own application), F8.18 (the two grounds of 33(5) and the two times).

§ `Part 8 -- Appeals to Charity Tribunal`

§§ `Article 32 -- Establishment of Charity Tribunal`

-- Article 32 is inert: it establishes a body and declares its function, and nothing in it is computed.  The Tribunal is the actor `the Charity Tribunal` of the regulative rules below;
-- the appeal rights are in Articles 33 to 35; Schedule 2 (G9) makes further provision.
-- src:685 | 32 Establishment of Charity Tribunal
-- src:686 | (1) There is established a tribunal to be known as the Charity Tribunal.
-- src:687 | (2) The function of the tribunal is to hear and determine appeals under this Part.
-- src:688 | (3) Schedule 2 makes further provision in respect of the tribunal.

§§ `Article 33 -- Persons who may appeal and decisions that may be appealed`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 33(1): an applicant for registration
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `33(1) -- an applicant for registration`

-- src:690 | (1) An applicant for registration may appeal against a decision of the Commissioner –
-- src:691 | (a) to refuse to register the applicant; or
-- src:692 | (b) to refuse to register the applicant in the restricted section of the register.
@ref Article 33(1)(a) (src:691)
GIVEN appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(1)(a) an applicant for registration appeals a refusal to register the applicant` appeal MEANS
        appeal's appellant's `an applicant for registration`
    AND appeal's `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner refuses`

@ref Article 33(1)(b) (src:692)
GIVEN appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(1)(b) an applicant for registration appeals a refusal to register the applicant in the restricted section` appeal MEANS
        appeal's appellant's `an applicant for registration`
    AND appeal's `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to enter a charity in the restricted section, Article 9(6) and (7)`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner refuses`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 33(2): a registered charity
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `33(2) -- a registered charity: five decisions`

-- F8.16.  "(a) to deregister the charity": a decision to deregister under Article 16 is plainly one.  A deregistration granted on the charity's own application under Article 15(3)(a) is
-- also "a decision of the Commissioner to deregister the charity".  Reading A (taken): it is within (a), the words not distinguishing why; reading B: it is not, the charity having asked for it.
-- A REFUSAL to deregister under Article 15(3)(b) is not a decision to deregister on either reading (trap T12; IP32).
-- src:693 | (2) A registered charity may appeal against a decision of the Commissioner –
-- src:694 | (a) to deregister the charity;
-- src:695 | (b) to refuse permission, under Article 12(4), for the charity to change its registered name or add an alternative registered name;
-- src:696 | (c) to require the charity, under Article 12(6), to apply to change its registered name;
-- src:697 | (d) to refuse approval, under Article 13(3), of a proposed amendment of the charity’s purposes to add or substitute a different charitable purpose; or
-- src:698 | (e) to refuse to approve an amendment, proposed under Article 13(4)(b), to the charity’s registered public benefit statement.
@ref Article 33(2)(a) (src:694)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.16 is the one read here)
      appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(2)(a) a registered charity appeals a decision to deregister the charity` interp appeal MEANS
        appeal's appellant's `a registered charity`
    AND appeal's `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
    AND (   appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to deregister a charity in other cases, Article 16`
         OR (    appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)`
             AND interp's `whether Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration on the charity's own application` EQUALS `Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration granted on the charity's own application` ))

@ref Article 33(2)(b) (src:695)
GIVEN appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(2)(b) a registered charity appeals a refusal of permission to change or add a registered name` appeal MEANS
        appeal's appellant's `a registered charity`
    AND appeal's `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to permit a change or addition of registered name, Article 12(4)`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner refuses`

@ref Article 33(2)(c) (src:696)
GIVEN appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(2)(c) a registered charity appeals a requirement to apply to change its registered name` appeal MEANS
        appeal's appellant's `a registered charity`
    AND appeal's `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to require a charity to apply to change its registered name, Article 12(6)`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`

@ref Article 33(2)(d) (src:697)
GIVEN appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(2)(d) a registered charity appeals a refusal of approval of an amendment of its purposes` appeal MEANS
        appeal's appellant's `a registered charity`
    AND appeal's `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner refuses`

@ref Article 33(2)(e) (src:698)
GIVEN appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(2)(e) a registered charity appeals a refusal to approve an amendment of its registered public benefit statement` appeal MEANS
        appeal's appellant's `a registered charity`
    AND appeal's `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner refuses`

-- F8.4.  The list of 33(2) is closed on reading A (taken); on reading B an unlisted decision of the same kind as a listed one is appealable by analogy.  The two analogues the trap T12 names
-- (T12): a registered charity's refused request for entry in the restricted section (Article 9(7); compare 33(1)(b), which gives the same decision to an applicant), and a charity's refused
-- application to deregister (Article 15(3)(b); compare 33(2)(a)).  Every other unlisted decision stays unappealable on both readings.
@ref Article 33(2) (src:693-698)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.4 is the one read here)
      appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(2) by analogy with Article 33(1)(b): a registered charity appeals a refusal of its request for entry in the restricted section` interp appeal MEANS
        interp's `whether the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed` EQUALS `a decision unlisted in Article 33 is appealable by analogy with a listed one`
    AND appeal's appellant's `a registered charity`
    AND appeal's `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to enter a charity in the restricted section, Article 9(6) and (7)`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner refuses`

@ref Article 33(2) (src:693-698)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.4 is the one read here)
      appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(2) by analogy with Article 33(2)(a): a registered charity appeals a refusal to deregister it on its own application` interp appeal MEANS
        interp's `whether the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed` EQUALS `a decision unlisted in Article 33 is appealable by analogy with a listed one`
    AND appeal's appellant's `a registered charity`
    AND appeal's `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner refuses`

