§§§ `33(3) -- a person on whom the Commissioner serves a notice under Article 26 or a required steps notice`

-- src:699 | (3) A person on whom the Commissioner serves a notice under Article 26 or a required steps notice may appeal against the decision of the Commissioner to impose a requirement contained in the notice.
@ref Article 33(3) (src:699)
GIVEN appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(3) a person served with the notice appeals the decision to impose a requirement in it` appeal MEANS
        appeal's appellant's `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement`
    AND (   appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to impose a requirement contained in a notice under Article 26`
         OR appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to impose a requirement contained in a required steps notice` )
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`

