§§§ `33(5) -- any other person, against a decision to register an applicant`

-- F8.13.  "A person, other than an applicant for registration, a registered charity, or the Attorney General".  Reading A (taken): any applicant for registration and any registered charity is
-- excluded - the three classes already have their own appeals in 33(1), (2) and (4) - so a registered charity with an interest in a similar name cannot use 33(5).  Reading B: only the applicant
-- whose application is decided, the charity it became, and the Attorney General are excluded.
-- src:701 | (5) A person, other than an applicant for registration, a registered charity, or the Attorney General, may appeal against a decision of the Commissioner to register an applicant, on the ground that, at both the time of the application and the time of the appeal –
-- src:702 | (a) the applicant did not meet the charity test; or
-- src:703 | (b) if the appellant has an interest in the registered name of the applicant, that name was undesirable under Article 12(1).
@ref Article 33(5) (src:701)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.13 is the one read here)
      appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(5) the appellant is a person other than those excluded` interp appeal MEANS
        NOT appeal's appellant's `the Attorney General`
    AND CONSIDER interp's `who is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)`
        WHEN `any applicant for registration or registered charity is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)` THEN
            NOT (appeal's appellant's `an applicant for registration` OR appeal's appellant's `a registered charity`)
        WHEN `only the applicant concerned and the charity it became are excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)` THEN
            NOT (    appeal's `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration`
                 AND (appeal's appellant's `an applicant for registration` OR appeal's appellant's `a registered charity`))

-- F8.18.  "on the ground that, at both the time of the application and the time of the appeal - (a) the applicant did not meet the charity test; or (b) if the appellant has an interest in the
-- registered name of the applicant, that name was undesirable under Article 12(1)".  Reading A (taken): each ground must hold at both times - (a) at both, or (b) at both.  Reading B: some ground
-- must hold at each time - (a) or (b) at the time of the application, and (a) or (b) at the time of the appeal.  (b) is open only to an appellant with an interest in the name.
@ref Article 33(5)(a) (src:702)
GIVEN `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9: whether the applicant met the charity test at the time of the application
      `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9: whether the applicant meets the charity test at the time of the appeal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(5)(a) the applicant did not meet the charity test at both times` `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` MEANS
        NOT `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application`
    AND NOT `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal`

@ref Article 33(5)(b) (src:703)
GIVEN appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18: whether the applicant's name was undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18: whether the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(5)(b) the appellant has an interest in the name and it was undesirable at both times` appeal `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal` MEANS
        appeal's appellant's `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant`
    AND `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application`
    AND `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal`

@ref Article 33(5) (src:701-703)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.18 is the one read here)
      appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
      `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9
      `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(5) a ground holds at the two times` interp appeal `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how the two grounds of Article 33(5) combine with the two times`
    WHEN `each ground of Article 33(5) must hold at both times` THEN
            `Art 33(5)(a) the applicant did not meet the charity test at both times` `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal`
        OR  `Art 33(5)(b) the appellant has an interest in the name and it was undesirable at both times` appeal `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal`
    WHEN `some ground of Article 33(5) must hold at each of the two times` THEN
            (   NOT `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application`
             OR (appeal's appellant's `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` AND `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application`))
        AND (   NOT `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal`
             OR (appeal's appellant's `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` AND `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal`))

@ref Article 33(5) (src:701-703)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.13 and F8.18 are the ones read here)
      appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
      `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9
      `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 33(5) a person other than the applicant, a registered charity or the Attorney General appeals a decision to register an applicant` interp appeal `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal` MEANS
        `Art 33(5) the appellant is a person other than those excluded` interp appeal
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s subject EQUALS `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`
    AND appeal's `decision appealed`'s outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
    AND `Art 33(5) a ground holds at the two times` interp appeal `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal`

