§§§ `33 -- which paragraph gives the right, if any`

-- The paragraphs are tried in the Law's order; the first that applies is named.  The last answer, "no appeal is given by Part 8", is not a statement that no other remedy exists
-- (Article 40(1) preserves the independent powers of the Attorney General, the Bailiff and the court).
@ref Article 33 (src:690-703)
@export Which paragraph of Article 33, if any, gives the appellant a right to appeal the decision of the Commissioner (default - the list of decisions is closed, so an unlisted decision gets 'no appeal is given by Part 8'); for a third party's appeal against a registration, the charity test and the name are asked at the time of the application and at the time of the appeal
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.4, F8.13, F8.16 and F8.18 are the ones read here)
      appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing, against what decision (its subject and outcome - IP27), and whether the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration
      `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9: only read for a third party's appeal under Article 33(5)
      `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9: only read for a third party's appeal under Article 33(5)
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18: only read for a third party's appeal under Article 33(5)
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18: only read for a third party's appeal under Article 33(5)
GIVETH A `Right of appeal under Article 33`
`Art 33 the right of appeal` interp appeal `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 33(1)(a) an applicant for registration appeals a refusal to register the applicant` appeal
        THEN `a right of appeal under Article 33(1)(a)`
        IF `Art 33(1)(b) an applicant for registration appeals a refusal to register the applicant in the restricted section` appeal
        THEN `a right of appeal under Article 33(1)(b)`
        IF `Art 33(2)(a) a registered charity appeals a decision to deregister the charity` interp appeal
        THEN `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(a)`
        IF `Art 33(2)(b) a registered charity appeals a refusal of permission to change or add a registered name` appeal
        THEN `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(b)`
        IF `Art 33(2)(c) a registered charity appeals a requirement to apply to change its registered name` appeal
        THEN `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(c)`
        IF `Art 33(2)(d) a registered charity appeals a refusal of approval of an amendment of its purposes` appeal
        THEN `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(d)`
        IF `Art 33(2)(e) a registered charity appeals a refusal to approve an amendment of its registered public benefit statement` appeal
        THEN `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(e)`
        IF `Art 33(3) a person served with the notice appeals the decision to impose a requirement in it` appeal
        THEN `a right of appeal under Article 33(3)`
        IF `Art 33(4) the Attorney General appeals a decision of the Commissioner` appeal
        THEN `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`
        IF `Art 33(5) a person other than the applicant, a registered charity or the Attorney General appeals a decision to register an applicant` interp appeal `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal`
        THEN `Art 33(5) which ground` appeal `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal`
        IF `Art 33(2) by analogy with Article 33(1)(b): a registered charity appeals a refusal of its request for entry in the restricted section` interp appeal
        THEN `a right of appeal by analogy with Article 33(1)(b)`
        IF `Art 33(2) by analogy with Article 33(2)(a): a registered charity appeals a refusal to deregister it on its own application` interp appeal
        THEN `a right of appeal by analogy with Article 33(2)(a)`
        OTHERWISE `no appeal is given by Part 8`

-- The sub-paragraph of 33(5) that carries the right: (a) if the charity test failed at both times, else (b) if the name was undesirable at both, else (reading B only) a mixture of the two.
@ref Article 33(5) (src:701-703)
GIVEN appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing and against what decision
      `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9
      `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18
GIVETH A `Right of appeal under Article 33`
`Art 33(5) which ground` appeal `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 33(5)(a) the applicant did not meet the charity test at both times` `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal`
        THEN `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(a)`
        IF `Art 33(5)(b) the appellant has an interest in the name and it was undesirable at both times` appeal `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the application` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1) at the time of the appeal`
        THEN `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(b)`
        OTHERWISE `a right of appeal under Article 33(5) on grounds that differ between the two times`

